ast, us-west, and eu-west. The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). Retrying the rollback completed successfully. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until root cause is understood."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MxfYU9gh6bHXesHg6i713x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18). The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release that was failing health checks. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the fleet mixed. Retrying the same rollback completed cleanly.\n- **Incident:** The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. The incident had been created, so I did not open a duplicate. It is SEV2 and describes the failure, the rollback, the partial failure, and the post-rollback status.\n\nFollow-ups for the team:\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure.\n- Look into the orchestrator partial failure, since it could recur on the next rollback.\n- Don't redeploy v2.3.1 until the cause is understood.", "type": "text"}]